# ======================
# Tuning manifests
# ======================
# generate_tuning_configs.py resolves every path at generation time and
# writes them absolute, so a manifest is bound to the machine that made it:
# one written here sends the cluster's array tasks to /Users/... and fails
# all of them. Regenerate it wherever the sweep runs --
#
#     python scripts/generate_tuning_configs.py <spec> --overwrite
#
# The spec, the base config and the generated cell configs are tracked, so
# the manifest is reproducible from them and nothing is lost by its absence.
TransEHR2/configs/experiments/tuning/*_manifest.yaml
# Phase 2's bases are the phase-1 winners' own configs, written by
# select_tuned_cell.py. Derived from a ranking, like the manifests.
# phase1_base.yaml is tracked: it is the authored centre of phase 1.
TransEHR2/configs/experiments/tuning/phase[2-9]*_base.yaml
